        "language": "english",
        "review": "Its hard for me to write this as a negative review, as i adore this game, and have countless hours spent on it as a kid.\nAs i heard the announcement for the remaster i was really exicted, to revisit one of my favourite childhood games again with a modern touch.\n\nI have to say i expected more than just improved visuals, when the original is still free.\nThe bare minimum for me would be:\n- more FPS than the current locked 30 fps cap\n- functioning multiplayer/coop\n- steam workshop / mod support\n- controller support\n\nMultiplayer was added using the steam api, but it does not function well:\n- You have to manually select frame latency\n- Depending on distance between the host, the game runs on slow motion or there is a significant delay \n   between inputs, making in unplayable.\n- Can't go back to main menu from online lobby, you have to relaunch the game\n\nI really love this game. but sadly i cannot recommend the game in its current state.\n\np.s forgot to mention there is also no cloud save?",
